							"settings": {
								"tabs": [
									{
										"_id": "0b33c41",
										"tab_title": "Do I need my passport to travel?",
										"tab_content": "<p>Yes. Tickets are issued against a passport and identity is checked at the station, so travel with the document you booked with.</p>"
									},
									{
										"_id": "9b8fe80",
										"tab_title": "How far ahead should I book?",
										"tab_content": "<p>As far ahead as you reasonably can for peak season and holiday periods, when popular services fill. Outside those, availability is easier.</p>"
									},
									{
										"_id": "8f9eb48",
										"tab_title": "How far is the station from town?",
										"tab_content": "<p>It varies by station and several are a substantial drive from the town centre. Plan the transfer at both ends as part of the journey.</p>"
									},
									{
										"_id": "6b5cf8d",
										"tab_title": "Can Brother Tours book tickets for me?",
										"tab_content": "<p>We assist travellers with rail arrangements as part of a journey. Tell us your dates and route and we will advise on what is possible.</p>"
									},
									{
										"_id": "7778523",
										"tab_title": "What can I take on board?",
										"tab_content": "<p>Luggage allowances and a restricted-item list apply, broadly comparable to air travel. These change, so check the current rules close to your travel date.</p>"
									},
									{
										"_id": "4657b04",
										"tab_title": "Is the railway better than flying or driving?",
										"tab_content": "<p>On the Vientiane–Vang Vieng–Luang Prabang corridor it is usually the best option once transfer time is counted. For other routes, not always — we advise per itinerary.</p>"
									}
								],
